---
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import openfireImg from '../assets/open-source/openfire.png';
import openfireImgLight from '../assets/open-source/openfire-light.png';
import dockerImg from '../assets/open-source/docker.png';
import dockerImgLight from '../assets/open-source/docker-light.png';
import reviewLoopImg from '../assets/open-source/review-loop.png';
import reviewLoopImgLight from '../assets/open-source/review-loop-light.png';
---

<section id="open-source" aria-label="Open source work" class="pt-14 pb-10 sm:pt-20 sm:pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 data-animate="fade-up" class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-6">Work in the Open</h2>
        <p data-animate="fade-up" class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-16">
            Most of my work is behind closed doors, but not all of it. Openfire gives a good glimpse into how I
            work — the pull requests and discussions show how I collaborate with engineers across time zones and take
            care with software that many organisations depend on. Review-Loop is something different, a tool I built
            from scratch, developing and experimenting openly with AI without the constraints of a sensitive codebase.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            {/* Openfire */}
            <div
                    data-animate="fade-up"
                    class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-subtle rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-8 relative overflow-hidden min-h-[220px] card-hover"
            >
                <div class="absolute -bottom-4 -right-4 w-[200px] h-[200px] opacity-[0.12] pointer-events-none">
                    <Image src={openfireImg} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full dark-only"/>
                    <Image src={openfireImgLight} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full light-only"/>
                </div>
                <div class="relative z-10">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Openfire</h3>
                    <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4 md:pr-8">
                        The open source XMPP server used by defence and government organisations across the world. I'm a
                        long time contributor, my contributions include replacing the core networking framework with
                        Netty, a systematic cryptographic security programme, introducing Architecture Decision Records,
                        and performance engineering.
                    </p>
                    <a
                            href="https://github.com/igniterealtime/Openfire"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="inline-block text-sm text-accent-functional hover:text-accent-light transition-colors break-words external-link"
                    >
                        igniterealtime/Openfire<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            {/* Openfire Docker Compose */}
            <div
                    data-animate="fade-up"
                    class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-subtle rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-8 relative overflow-hidden min-h-[220px] card-hover"
            >
                <div class="absolute -bottom-4 -right-4 w-[200px] h-[200px] opacity-[0.12] pointer-events-none">
                    <Image src={dockerImg} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full dark-only"/>
                    <Image src={dockerImgLight} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full light-only"/>
                </div>
                <div class="relative z-10">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Openfire Docker Compose</h3>
                    <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4 md:pr-8">
                        I created this Docker Compose environment for running multiple Openfire servers
                        with databases during local development and testing. It's since been adopted by
                        several of the Openfire core developers and testers. I've added clustering support,
                        OCSP configuration, Java remote debugging, and comprehensive documentation.
                    </p>
                    <a
                            href="https://github.com/surevine/openfire-docker-compose"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="inline-block text-sm text-accent-functional hover:text-accent-light transition-colors break-words external-link"
                    >
                        surevine/openfire-docker-compose<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            {/* review-loop */}
            <div
                    data-animate="fade-up"
                    class="md:col-span-2 bg-bg-surface border border-border-subtle rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-8 relative overflow-hidden min-h-[220px] card-hover"
            >
                <div class="absolute -bottom-4 -right-4 w-[200px] h-[200px] opacity-[0.12] pointer-events-none">
                    <Image src={reviewLoopImg} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full dark-only"/>
                    <Image src={reviewLoopImgLight} alt="" width={200} height={200} loading="lazy"
                           class="object-contain w-full h-full light-only"/>
                </div>
                <div class="relative z-10">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Review-Loop</h3>
                    <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4 md:pr-8">
                        A tool I built to bridge human reviewers and AI coding agents. Annotate your rendered
                        site in-browser (select text, highlight elements, write notes) and your agent reads the
                        feedback directly via MCP, edits the source, and reports back for your approval (or not!).
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4 md:pr-8">
                        Building review-loop in the open gives me the freedom to fully explore AI-enhanced software
                        engineering without the constraints of a commercial or sensitive codebase. Experimenting with
                        the same engineering rigour and practices, but also pushing the boundaries of speed,
                        tooling, and working practices in ways that other projects don't always allow.
                    </p>
                    <a
                            href="https://github.com/viv/review-loop"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="inline-block text-sm text-accent-functional hover:text-accent-light transition-colors break-words external-link"
                    >
                        viv/review-loop<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {/* GitHub profile link */}
        <p data-animate="fade-up" class="mt-10 text-text-secondary text-sm">
            More at <a
                href="https://github.com/viv"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-accent-functional hover:text-accent-light transition-colors external-link"
        >github.com/viv<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
